    "result_text": "All tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature following the existing \"derived read-only field\" pattern already used throughout this codebase (e.g. `telephoneDisplay`, `displayName`, `membershipNumber`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `title` field (column, getter, setter) and a `@Transient getSalutation()` deriving `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just `lastName` when no title is present (matching the neighboring derived getters' style).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `title` as an optional input property on `OwnerFields` (enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`) and `salutation` as a `readOnly` derived property on `Owner`. The MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks both up by name automatically (no mapper changes needed), just like the other derived fields.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table so the persisted title round-trips through create \u2192 GET.\n\nThe logic lives in the domain model where the other name-derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) already live, so no controller or catch-all class grew.",
